# Git Workflow

- Create a feature branch before substantial changes.
- Name branches using the format: `<ticket-number>/<short-description>` (e.g. `PSS-123/fix-auth-redirect`).
- Only prepend `th/` to the branch name if the user explicitly requests it (e.g. "prepend with th").
- Use conventional commit prefixes: `feat:`, `fix:`, `chore:`, `docs:`.
- Ask for confirmation before push, merge, rebase, or reset.
- Before committing, run `pnpm lint` and fix any reported issues.
- Do NOT add "Made-with: Cursor", "Made with Cursor", "Made with Claude", or any AI attribution to commit messages or PR descriptions.
- When creating a PR, ask the user: "Is there a Linear ticket number for this PR? (e.g. PSS-123, leave blank to skip)". If provided, include a plain link at the bottom of the PR body: `[TICKET](https://linear.app/your-org/issue/TICKET)`. If blank, omit it entirely.
- When creating a PR, include:
  - A short summary of what changed and why
  - A test plan with commands or manual verification steps
